<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>00NATION DOUBLES UP REVENUES FROM Q1-22 TO Q1-23, NEW MANAGEMENT, TALENT AND MORE</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2023-03-02 18:01:28</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>00NATION continues the growth trajectory and doubles up revenues from NOK 6,150K in Q1 2022 to NOK 14,896K in Q1-23. The majority of revenues were from commercial partners, with a significant bump in talent and esports revenues<br> <br>"We have proven our creative, production and execution capabilities over some time now and we’ll push hard to keep the pace up on the media side. It’s one of the four cornerstones to our business and the one we’ve initially focused on, so naturally, that's where we’ve seen the biggest progress. We’re also well organized and sizable enough to lift the focus and have recently placed more effort and resources into the other cornerstones. The talent department is seeing rapid development, we’ve started to roll out the brand and build community, and esports is steadily improving. Like we’ve always said; we build business first, then the brand and then the community with increased presence and investment into esports over time. We live and execute by that plan.” - Sebastian Geurts (CEO)<br><br><br>00NATION is delighted to welcome to the Board Runar Eidsaa (as Chairman) and Carlos Eduardo Cunha (Kadu) replacing Magnus Halvorsen and Stian Blipp. Runar has extensive experience in business management and board roles in Norway and Kadu in businesses in the US and S.America. Along with the current member Dariusz Mioduski, each will bring a unique and proactive contribution to 00NATION<br><br>“I have been watching 00Nation with interest and growing excitement over the last year, and tracking their progress. When I was invited to join the Board as Chairman I was truly honoured and proud to be helping out creating the new media house of the future . Its a great team and a great vision and I know its going to be an amazing journey” Runar Eidsaa (Chairman of the Board)<br><br><br>00NATION recent changes to management are the following: Stein Willmann is replaced by Christian Aass, and Steffen Willumsen is replaced by Elin Haukvik. Christian (previously TRY) has been around since September 2021 and Elin (previously Splay) has been around since September 2022. This concludes the management with the following team: Sebastian Geurts (CEO), Christian Aass (COO), Mats Vigeland (CMO), Paul Davis (Head of talent and PR), David Williams (Head of business affairs and investor relations), Elin Haukvik (Head of commercial partnerships), Adrian Le Dantec (Head of special projects), Ricardo Sinigaglia (Head of gaming and esports). <br><br>"In a fast paced environment, changes are natural. We are thankful for the time we had together. 00NATION has become a popular place to work and we are not only seeing evolution on a top level, CVs are pouring in and the entire organization is seeing a continuous uplift. It's been a challenging but giving journey so so far and it's a pleasure to work side by side with Sebastian and his creative intellect and extreme drive” - Christian Aass, (COO)<br><br><br>00NATION signs Øystein Holt (previously Unicare, Power, Idex Biometrics, BDO ) as new CFO, starting June 1st 2023.<br>"I'm thrilled to be joining the amazing 00NATION team! Joining a fast-paced and dynamic startup has always been a dream of mine. The company's lean startup culture is a perfect fit, and I'm excited to be a part of a team that's achieved so much in just over a year. I can't wait to contribute to their growth and success. Let's keep the momentum going, have some fun along the way, and achieve great things together.” - Øystein Holt, CFO 00NATION<br><br><br><br>- Mr Savage (professional fortnite player and Internet personality with 10M+ followers) joined 00NATION in February<br> <br>"Over the last year, I’ve been following a new, very exciting project that has a real shot at being the next big thing: 00NATION. The timing was finally there and I’m finally home! I've had a lot of offers, but this is it. Insane skills. Insane team. Dope brands. Good vibes and sick projects. And they didn’t disappoint. What a good start." - Mr Savage<br> <br>- 00 launched its first branded series with «The 00 SQUAD» featuring Truls Torp and Kim «minikim» Knutsen, and are 8 episodes deep, aggregating over 350 000 views and 7 000 subscribers, with multiple commercial executions including Hugo Boss and Coca Cola during the first month, with overwhelmingly positive response from the community. <br> <br>"Ever since we joined 00NATION, it’s been an absolute blast. The management is incredible, the support is there 24/7, and we already see the enormous potential unlocking. We have everything we need. It’s in our hands and up to the creative work and the hours we put in, and we got a real shot at breaking through on the internet. We are already on a roll and we will never stop before we have hit vision" - Kim Knutsen and Truls Torp<br> <br>Other recent news:<br><br>- Aleksander Aurdal joins as executive producer (previously Motion blur, Aparent, worked with clients such as DNB, IKEA, Spotify) <br>- Ziwer Tali joins as talent manager (previously GR:OW with talent such as Amanda Delara, Sondre Haftorsen, Sei Selina) <br>- XBOX and 00NATION wins prize for best activation during DreamHack Winter in Sweden<br>- 00 GameNights ends the series of pilots with a full house, successful activations (Xbox, Oreo). Ready to launch pre summer<br>- Capcom praises 00NATION activation during its last Street Fighter 5 major event<br>- The counter-strike team qualifies for ESL pro league <br> <br>Follow @zerozeronation on instagram for frequent updates:<br><br>Contact:<br><br>Investor relations: <br>David Williams (dw@00nation.com)<br> <br>Media and PR: <br>Paul Davis (pd@00nation.com)</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
&nbsp;
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
