<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>NORDAVIND AS – NOK 50 MILLION PRIVATE PLACEMENT SUCCESFULLY COMPLETED</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-07-07 09:24:59</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>NOT FOR RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION, IN WHOLE OR IN PART DIRECTLY OR INDIRECTLY, IN AUSTRALIA, CANADA, JAPAN, HONG KONG OR THE UNITED STATES OR ANY OTHER JURISDICTION IN WHICH THE RELEASE, PUBLICATION OR DISTRIBUTION WOULD BE UNLAWFUL. THIS ANNOUNCEMENT DOES NOT CONSTITUTE AN OFFER OF ANY OF THE SECURITIES DESCRIBED HEREIN.<br><br>Oslo, 7 July 2021. <br><br>Reference is made to the press release from Nordavind AS (“Nordavind” or the “Company”) published on 6 July 2021 regarding a contemplated private placement (the “Private Placement”) and Merger with 00Nation (the “Merger”).<br><br>Nordavind is pleased to announce that the Private Placement has been successfully completed. The Private Placement consisted of 3,333,333 offer shares (the “Offer Shares”) at a subscription price of NOK 15.0 per share (the “Offer Price”) raising gross proceeds for the Company of approximately NOK 50 million.<br><br>The Private Placement attracted very strong interest from high-quality investors and family offices, and was multiple times oversubscribed. As a result of the strong interest, Nordavind decided to end the application period earlier than initially anticipated.<br><br>The transaction was well supported by both founders, board and management who subscribed for a total of NOK 15 million.<br><br>The net proceeds of the Private Placement will be used to for payment of the cash consideration under the share purchase agreement relating to the shares of 00Nation, and the remainder will be used to fund growth investments and for general corporate purposes.<br><br>Completion of the Private Placement is conditional upon (i) all necessary corporate resolutions for consummating the Private Placement being validly made by the Company, including without limitation (a) resolution by the Company's board of directors to proceed with the Private Placement and (b) approval of the share capital increase and issue of the New Shares required for completion of the Private Placement by the Company’s extraordinary general meeting (the “EGM”); (ii) the allocated New Shares having been fully paid; and (iii) registration of the share capital increase pertaining to the New Shares with the Norwegian Register of Business Enterprises and issuance of the New Shares with VPS.<br><br>Notification of conditional allocation will be communicated to investors on or about 7 July 2021. The EGM will be held on or about 15 July 2021. The payment date is expected on or about 16 July 2021, subject to the Private Placement being approved. Delivery of the offer shares will be made as soon as practically possible after the registration of the capital increase with the Norwegian Register of Business Enterprises.<br><br>The Company would like to thank all investors who subscribed for shares in the Private Placement for their vote of vote of confidence.<br><br>Advisors:<br><br>Arctic Securities AS and SpareBank 1 Markets AS are engaged as Joint Lead Managers and Joint Bookrunners in connection with the Private Placement. Ro Sommernes advokatfirma is acting as legal advisor to the Company.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.nordavind.gg">
http://www.nordavind.gg</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Nordavind and 00Nation merges to form a global esports & youth culture powerhouse and contemplated private placement</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-07-06 07:37:37</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>The business combination will amplify revenue potential across existing revenue models, adding new revenue streams from talent management, content formats and subscription-based activities.<br><br>Oslo, Norway, July 06, 2021 <br>Nordavind, a leading esports organization, today announces it has entered an agreement to acquire 00Nation to form a global esports and youth culture powerhouse.  <br><br>The founders of 00Nation, who were instrumental in building FaZe Clan from a niche YouTube sensation to a global brand with $200M enterprise value, will join the senior management team of Nordavind, with Sebastian Geurts assuming the role as CEO for the combined entity. <br><br>Together, Nordavind and 00Nation will build a global lifestyle community centered around esports and gaming, working with talent across music, arts, tv/film, fashion and sports.  The combined entity will launch several subscription-based concepts, including a gaming league, talk shows, as well as live exhibitions and events. <br><br>The acquisition comes at a time where esports & gaming have eclipsed the music industry as the most important aspect of youth culture. Esports & gaming’s status in the broader mainstream culture is exemplified through footballer Arthur Melo’s pre-commitment to Nordavind in the upcoming capital raise.<br><br>"I have followed gaming and esports since I was a kid and been offered many opportunities to join different organizations, but it never felt like the right fit. 00Nation is the first time I have ever felt goosebumps. The team, talent and mix of investors is powerful, and the combination of a winning culture, the branding, the activities, and the real and authentic approach to the youth; it is incredible. I’m coming in as an investor and I will also be joining the team to help develop the brand and the community.” - Arthur Melo, Professional football player for Juventus and Brazil<br><br>“We’re excited to combine our team’s experience across entertainment, esports and youth culture together with Nordavind to break into youth culture and go global. You can have the best ideas in the world, but it comes down to one thing in the end: People. I am proud to have such a strong team around me, both people that I have teamed up with for years, and relatively new faces. The combined team have the mindset, know-how and experience to execute the vision.” - Sebastian Geurts, CEO at 00Nation<br><br>“The most successful and valuable esports organizations in the world are those that have built communities which merge gaming and esports with arts, music, fashion and tv/film. Through this business combination, we are combining Nordavind’s strong position within esport and gaming, with an organization whose team has a stellar track record in building global communities and concepts engaging youth and young adults. I have great belief that the combined entity has what it takes to deliver on our mutual vision to create a youth culture power house ” – Magnus Halvorsen, Chairman at Nordavind AS <br><br><br>The Private Placement<br>The acquisition of 100% of 00Nation will be settled through the issuance of 2,833,333 shares in Nordavind, as well as a cash consideration of approx. NOK 12 million. <br><br>As a part of the transaction, Nordavind will conduct a private placement of up to NOK 50 million in new shares (the “New Shares”) at NOK 15 per share (the “Private Placement”). The net proceeds from the Private Placement will be used for payment of the cash consideration under the share purchase agreement relating to the shares of 00Nation, and the remainder will be used to fund growth investments and for general corporate purposes.  <br><br>MH Capital AS (controlled by Magnus Halvorsen, chairman) has pre-committed to subscribe for NOK 10 million of New Shares. <br><br>The application period in the Private Placement starts today, 6 July 2021, at 09:00 CEST and ends at 16:30 CEST on 7 July 2021. The Company may at its sole discretion extend or shorten the application period at any time and for any reason.<br><br>The final number of New Shares to be issued and allocated will be made by the Company's Board of Directors at its sole discretion at the end of the application period. Notification of the allocation is expected to be sent by the Managers on or about 8 July 2021. The payment date for the Private Placement is expected to be on or about 16 July 2021 and the New Shares will we delivered as soon as possible after registration of the capital increase resulting from the Private Placement with the Norwegian Register of Business Enterprises. <br><br>Completion of the Private Placement is subject to the following conditions (the "Conditions"): (i) all necessary corporate resolutions for consummating the Private Placement being validly made by the Company, including without limitation (a) resolution by the Company's board of directors to proceed with the Private Placement and (b) approval of the share capital increase and issue of the New Shares required for completion of the Private Placement by the Company’s extraordinary general meeting (the “EGM”); (ii) the allocated New Shares having been fully paid; and (iii) registration of the share capital increase pertaining to the New Shares with the Norwegian Register of Business Enterprises and issuance of the New Shares with VPS.<br><br>Arctic Securities AS and SpareBank 1 Markets AS are acting as Joint Bookrunners (together, the "Managers") in connection with the Private Placement. Ro Sommernes advokatfirma DA is acting as legal advisor to the Company.<br><br><br>Disclaimer<br>This press release is not for release, directly or indirectly, in or into any jurisdiction where such release, publication or distribution is unlawful (except in accordance with applicable laws). The information contained herein does not constitute an offer to sell or the solicitation of an offer to buy nor shall there be any sale of the securities referred to herein in any jurisdiction in which such offer, solicitation or sale would be unlawful prior to the registration, exemption from registration or qualification under the securities laws of any jurisdiction.<br><br><br>About 00Nation:<br>00Nation is a community, lifestyle and management company managing and building youth talent spanning the genres of over music, fashion, art, gaming and sports. Led by a core team with expertise and track record in marketing and branding, with a track record of global success in building youth communities, gaming and lifestyle brands. 00Nation creates innovative formats and activities and executes with talent across digital youth communities, gaming and lifestyle concepts. <br><br><br>About Nordavind:<br>Nordavind is the leading Norwegian based Nordic esports and gaming media organization headquartered in the Barcode district of Oslo, Norway.<br>Today, Nordavind is the home of Nordic championship caliber players and teams competing across several of the top esports titles around the globe, in addition to the talent division which represents some of the most popular content creators in Norway and Scandinavia. <br><br>With a rich history of 24 Norwegian Championship titles and World Championship medals in Hearthstone & Street Fighter, Nordavind is strategically placed as a leading brand at the intersection between competitive gaming, lifestyle and online youth culture.<br> <br><br>Contacts:<br>Magnus Halvorsen<br>Chairman of the Board, Nordavind AS<br>T +47 920 20 111<br>mh@2020bulkers.com<br><br>Stein Wilmann<br>Managing Director, Nordavind AS<br>T +47 467 45 484<br>wilmann@nordavind.gg</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.nordavind.gg">
http://www.nordavind.gg</a>
&nbsp;
</td>
</tr>
<tr><td colspan="3"><hr /></td></tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td><h2>Nordavind AS (NVD) – Norwegian Block Exchange partners with Nordavind for multi-year deal</h2></td>
<td><h3>Company news</h3></td>
<td align="right"><h3>2021-03-30 11:54:04</h3></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3"><p>Nordavind is pleased to announce a multi-year partnership with Norwegian Block Exchange (“NBX”), the leading Norwegian cryptocurrency exchange.<br><br>Under the partnership, NBX will target customer growth through Nordavind’s community of 4,3 followers. <br><br>NBX and Nordavind will also work together to introduce cryptocurrency in tournaments as well as new bonus and loyalty programs for players.<br><br>“This was a no-brainer, it was just a question of time. Cryptocurrency is here to stay, and young people will play a major role in the next wave of adoption, with both payment mechanisms and investment opportunities. E-sports and cryptocurrency are experiencing exponential growth, attracting audiences beyond just young people. We are very pleased that we have now entered into a partnership with Nordavind, where several of the players already are familiar with NBX. Therefore the timing is perfect for reaching out to each other and together create meaningful interactions for everyone who is interested in e-sports and the money of the future ", - says Stig Aleksander Kjos-Mathisen, CEO of Norwegian Block Exchange.<br><br>“Nordavind and NBX are two brands born in the digital world, which makes us a natural fit. Both cryptocurrency and e-sports are ground-breaking in their respective segments, and also share much of the same target area. We are proud to work with such a solid company as NBX, and we are eager to see what we can achieve together in the time to come ", - says Steffen Willumsen, Commercial Director for Nordavind<br><br>About NBX:<br>Norwegian Block Exchange is a Norwegian cryptocurrency exchange established in 2018 and launched publicly in April 2020. NBX makes it possible for both individuals and companies to buy and sell cryptocurrencies, including the most popular ones such as Bitcoin and Ethereum. NBX is part of Ledger Vault's insurance program, and is thus the only crypto exchange in the Nordic region that insures customers' funds. NBX closed an investment round of NOK 60 million in December 2020, which enables the company to become the first crypto bank in the Nordic region.<br>More information at nbx.com<br><br>About Nordavind:<br>Nordavind is the leading Nordic e-sports and gaming media organization based in Norway with headquarters in the Barcode district of Oslo. Today, Nordavind is home to Nordic players of championship caliber with teams competing for several of the most prestigious esports titles in the world. With 24 Norwegian Championship titles and World Cup medals in Hearthstone and Street Fighter, Nordavind is strategically placed as a leading organization at the intersection of e-sports, digital culture and new media entertainment.<br>More information at nordavind.gg<br><br>For further information, please contact:<br>Steffen Willumsen, Commercial Director Nordavind at +4794859356, or willumsen@nordavind.gg<br>Kateryna Dolzhenko, Marketing Manager, Norwegian Block Exchange at +4791907226 or kateryna.dolzhenko@nbx.com</p></td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top">
<td colspan="3" align="right">
<a target="_blank" href="http://www.nordavind.gg">
http://www.nordavind.gg</a>
&nbsp;
